{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776836303,"nonce":"clsEp+ROj2u0MIADKfFyfutWKHo=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABALaImQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/73","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat: enable S57 grid precompute (set robot_base_frame on s57_grids)","message":"## Problem\n\nAfter PR rolker/s57_tools#19/#20 lands, `s57_grids_node` supports a `robot_base_frame` parameter that enables eager chart precompute on first TF availability. With this enabled, the cold-cache startup wait (chart loads + initial tile regen, ~20–25 s today) is largely eliminated for the first plan after node activation.\n\nFor BizzyBoat, the relevant launch is `bizzyboat_project11/launch/core_launch.py:185-204` which already uses a `SetParameter` for `map_frame`. Adding two more `SetParameter` calls there (next to the existing one) is the minimal change.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd to the s57 `GroupAction`:\n\n```python\nSetParameter(name='robot_base_frame', value=[frame_prefix, 'base_link']),\nSetParameter(name='precompute_radius', value=5000.0),\n```\n\n`frame_prefix` resolves to `bizzy/` so the lookup target becomes `bizzy/base_link`. 5 km radius matches typical survey area (Portsmouth Harbor).\n\n## Why\n\nCold-cache analysis on the deadpool sim showed 11–26 s spent loading charts before the first plan can succeed. Same wait happens at boat startup. With precompute, charts are queued ~0.6 s after node activation, removing the chart-load contribution to first-plan latency. Verified end-to-end on sim 2026-04-22.\n\n## Requires\n\nrolker/s57_tools#19 / PR #20. No effect / no harm before that lands; the parameters are silently ignored.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Field validation on next BizzyBoat outing: log shows `Precompute enabled` and `Precompute: queued N of M charts within 5000 m of (lat, lon).` from `s57_grids_node` shortly after activation. Compare first-plan time vs current baseline.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}